{"data":"{\"thinking\":{\"type\":\"adaptive\"},\"stream\":true,\"tools\":[{\"description\":\"Read text with one-based inclusive start_line/end_line. Optional max_bytes bounds the read; job reports cap inline output and preserve the full result on disk.\",\"input_schema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"start_line\":{\"type\":\"integer\"},\"end_line\":{\"type\":\"integer\"},\"max_bytes\":{\"type\":\"integer\"}},\"required\":[\"path\"]},\"name\":\"read_file\"},{\"description\":\"List immediate entries, sorted by name; directories end with /.\",\"input_schema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"path\"]},\"name\":\"list_directory\"},{\"description\":\"Search files recursively using a regular expression. context_lines defaults to zero. Output uses grep path:line:text and path-line-context with merged windows.\",\"input_schema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"pattern\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"context_lines\":{\"type\":\"integer\"}},\"required\":[\"path\",\"pattern\"]},\"name\":\"search_files\"},{\"description\":\"Write text, creating parent directories. Existing files require overwrite:true unless append:true. Append preserves existing content.\",\"input_schema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"content\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"overwrite\":{\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"append\":{\"type\":\"boolean\"}},\"required\":[\"path\",\"content\"]},\"name\":\"write_file\"},{\"description\":\"Replace one exact, unique old_text anchor with new_text. Zero or multiple matches refuse without changing the file; read and provide a more specific anchor.\",\"input_schema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"old_text\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"new_text\":{\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"path\",\"old_text\",\"new_text\"]},\"name\":\"edit_file\"},{\"description\":\"Start a fresh /bin/sh in a PTY. cwd applies only to this call, relative to the workspace. Merged output and exit_code stay on disk; a running report is a handle, not cancellation. ai_callback_delay is seconds (default 3); pattern matches unseen output; max_output_bytes defaults to 16384.\",\"input_schema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"command\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"cwd\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"ai_callback_delay\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Seconds before looking again, default 3; never a job deadline\"},\"ai_callback_pattern\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Regex on unseen output\"},\"max_output_bytes\":{\"type\":\"integer\",\"description\":\"Inline output byte cap, default 16384\"}},\"required\":[\"command\"]},\"name\":\"run_command\"},{\"description\":\"Wait for a job, including a finished job. Return only unseen output; waiting does not stop execution.\",\"input_schema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"handle\":{\"type\":\"integer\"},\"ai_callback_delay\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Seconds before looking again, default 3; never a job deadline\"},\"ai_callback_pattern\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Regex on unseen output\"},\"max_output_bytes\":{\"type\":\"integer\",\"description\":\"Inline output byte cap, default 16384\"}},\"required\":[\"handle\"]},\"name\":\"wait_for_job\"},{\"description\":\"Send a line of input to a running PTY job, then wait. A missing trailing newline is added.\",\"input_schema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"handle\":{\"type\":\"integer\"},\"input\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"ai_callback_delay\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Seconds before looking again, default 3; never a job deadline\"},\"ai_callback_pattern\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Regex on unseen output\"},\"max_output_bytes\":{\"type\":\"integer\",\"description\":\"Inline output byte cap, default 16384\"}},\"required\":[\"handle\",\"input\"]},\"name\":\"send_input\"},{\"description\":\"Kill a job's process group. Go-only work is marked killed but its goroutine cannot be stopped.\",\"input_schema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"handle\":{\"type\":\"integer\"}},\"required\":[\"handle\"]},\"name\":\"kill_job\"},{\"description\":\"Set one-shot wait/output limits for the very next call, whichever tool it is. That call reports consumption; explicit call arguments override these limits.\",\"input_schema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"ai_callback_delay\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Seconds before looking again, default 3; never a job deadline\"},\"ai_callback_pattern\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Regex on unseen output\"},\"max_output_bytes\":{\"type\":\"integer\",\"description\":\"Inline output byte cap, default 16384\"}},\"required\":[]},\"name\":\"tool_limits\"},{\"description\":\"Checkpoint at a completed micro-goal. Write text with what succeeded, what failed, source locations and next steps. Removes all tool traffic but preserves conversation and this note.\",\"input_schema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"text\":{\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"text\"]},\"name\":\"micro_handoff\"},{\"description\":\"Keep the previous batch of tool results instead of automatic stubbing on supported models. Does not keep results of tools called alongside this call.\",\"input_schema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{}},\"name\":\"keep_tool_results\"}],\"model\":\"claude-haiku-5-5\",\"max_tokens\":4096,\"system\":\"You are a helpful assistant built from raw HTTP calls in Chapter 1 of The Art of Building AI Coding Agents. Answer briefly.\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"I worked on Cedar Lantern, release CL-721. I rejected automatic deletion of imported notes because support needs the originals when customers report mistakes. The replacement keeps source notes in an archive and stores accepted summaries separately. Every summary must preserve a source identifier. A failed summarization must leave the original note available. Default retention is thirty days.\\n\\nI moved cleanup from request arrival to an explicit completed-review boundary. The old coupling was the real hazard: any unrelated request could delete unreviewed work. Now nothing is removed until a person has finished reviewing it.\\n\\nMorgan owns archive review, scheduled for October 18.\\n\\nOpen question, not decided: whether attachments belong in the same archive or a separate one.\"}]},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"signature\":\"\",\"thinking\":\"\",\"type\":\"thinking\"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Got it. Here's what I have for Cedar Lantern CL-721:\\n\\n- **Deletion:** Automatic deletion of imported notes is rejected. Support needs originals for customer-reported mistakes.\\n- **Storage:** Source notes go to an archive. Accepted summaries are stored separately.\\n- **Summaries:** Each summary must preserve a source identifier.\\n- **Failure handling:** If summarization fails, the original note stays available.\\n- **Retention:** Default is 30 days.\\n- **Cleanup trigger:** Cleanup now runs at an explicit completed-review boundary, not on request arrival. Nothing is removed until a person finishes reviewing it.\\n- **Owner:** Morgan, archive review on October 18.\\n- **Open:** Whether attachments go in the same archive or a separate one. Not decided.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"This is a bounded memory exercise in an empty scratch workspace. Do not use filesystem or command tools. Analyze the supplied case, explain the decision briefly, then call micro_handoff exactly once with the important facts and reasons. After the tool returns, finish this turn without another tool call. Case two: The deployment rehearsal uses Harbor Finch, diagnostic tag HF-934. Priya owns the rehearsal scheduled for October 21. We rejected retrying a database migration automatically after a timeout: the remote operation may already have committed. The chosen procedure reads the migration ledger before deciding whether any retry is safe. The operator must retain the exact migration identifier and measured error, not a guess about success. We have not settled whether the ledger should live alongside application data or in a separate control database. The rollback package must remain available for seven days after deployment. Last week a log line said the worker stopped, but the child process was still alive and held the port open. The rehearsal now checks the child lifetime directly. Explain how this evidence changes the decision and checkpoint the completed analysis, preserving the unresolved question as unresolved.\"}]}]}","event":"request"}
