{"data":"{\"thinking\":{\"type\":\"adaptive\"},\"stream\":true,\"tools\":[{\"description\":\"Read text with one-based inclusive start_line/end_line. Optional max_bytes bounds the read; job reports cap inline output and preserve the full result on disk.\",\"input_schema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"start_line\":{\"type\":\"integer\"},\"end_line\":{\"type\":\"integer\"},\"max_bytes\":{\"type\":\"integer\"}},\"required\":[\"path\"]},\"name\":\"read_file\"},{\"description\":\"List immediate entries, sorted by name; directories end with /.\",\"input_schema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"path\"]},\"name\":\"list_directory\"},{\"description\":\"Search files recursively using a regular expression. context_lines defaults to zero. Output uses grep path:line:text and path-line-context with merged windows.\",\"input_schema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"pattern\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"context_lines\":{\"type\":\"integer\"}},\"required\":[\"path\",\"pattern\"]},\"name\":\"search_files\"},{\"description\":\"Write text, creating parent directories. Existing files require overwrite:true unless append:true. Append preserves existing content.\",\"input_schema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"content\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"overwrite\":{\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"append\":{\"type\":\"boolean\"}},\"required\":[\"path\",\"content\"]},\"name\":\"write_file\"},{\"description\":\"Replace one exact, unique old_text anchor with new_text. Zero or multiple matches refuse without changing the file; read and provide a more specific anchor.\",\"input_schema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"old_text\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"new_text\":{\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"path\",\"old_text\",\"new_text\"]},\"name\":\"edit_file\"},{\"description\":\"Start a fresh /bin/sh in a PTY. cwd applies only to this call, relative to the workspace. Merged output and exit_code stay on disk; a running report is a handle, not cancellation. ai_callback_delay is seconds (default 3); pattern matches unseen output; max_output_bytes defaults to 16384.\",\"input_schema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"command\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"cwd\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"ai_callback_delay\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Seconds before looking again, default 3; never a job deadline\"},\"ai_callback_pattern\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Regex on unseen output\"},\"max_output_bytes\":{\"type\":\"integer\",\"description\":\"Inline output byte cap, default 16384\"}},\"required\":[\"command\"]},\"name\":\"run_command\"},{\"description\":\"Wait for a job, including a finished job. Return only unseen output; waiting does not stop execution.\",\"input_schema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"handle\":{\"type\":\"integer\"},\"ai_callback_delay\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Seconds before looking again, default 3; never a job deadline\"},\"ai_callback_pattern\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Regex on unseen output\"},\"max_output_bytes\":{\"type\":\"integer\",\"description\":\"Inline output byte cap, default 16384\"}},\"required\":[\"handle\"]},\"name\":\"wait_for_job\"},{\"description\":\"Send a line of input to a running PTY job, then wait. A missing trailing newline is added.\",\"input_schema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"handle\":{\"type\":\"integer\"},\"input\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"ai_callback_delay\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Seconds before looking again, default 3; never a job deadline\"},\"ai_callback_pattern\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Regex on unseen output\"},\"max_output_bytes\":{\"type\":\"integer\",\"description\":\"Inline output byte cap, default 16384\"}},\"required\":[\"handle\",\"input\"]},\"name\":\"send_input\"},{\"description\":\"Kill a job's process group. Go-only work is marked killed but its goroutine cannot be stopped.\",\"input_schema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"handle\":{\"type\":\"integer\"}},\"required\":[\"handle\"]},\"name\":\"kill_job\"},{\"description\":\"Set one-shot wait/output limits for the very next call, whichever tool it is. That call reports consumption; explicit call arguments override these limits.\",\"input_schema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"ai_callback_delay\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Seconds before looking again, default 3; never a job deadline\"},\"ai_callback_pattern\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Regex on unseen output\"},\"max_output_bytes\":{\"type\":\"integer\",\"description\":\"Inline output byte cap, default 16384\"}},\"required\":[]},\"name\":\"tool_limits\"},{\"description\":\"Checkpoint at a completed micro-goal. Write text with what succeeded, what failed, source locations and next steps. Removes all tool traffic but preserves conversation and this note.\",\"input_schema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"text\":{\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"text\"]},\"name\":\"micro_handoff\"},{\"description\":\"Keep the previous batch of tool results instead of automatic stubbing on supported models. Does not keep results of tools called alongside this call.\",\"input_schema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{}},\"name\":\"keep_tool_results\"}],\"model\":\"claude-haiku-5-5\",\"max_tokens\":4096,\"system\":\"You are a helpful assistant built from raw HTTP calls in Chapter 1 of The Art of Building AI Coding Agents. Answer briefly.\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"I handled CL-721 (Cedar Lantern; Morgan owns archive review Oct 18): rejected auto-deleting imported notes. Archive originals; store accepted summaries separately, each with source ID; failed summarization keeps original. 30-day retention; cleanup only at explicit completed review, never on request arrival. Open: attachments same or separate archive. HF-934 (Harbor Finch; Priya, rehearsal Oct 21): rejected auto-retrying timed-out migration; check ledger, retry only if not completed; keep exact migration ID and error. Rollback kept 7 days. Verify child process state, not logs. Open: ledger in app or control DB. Rule: verify actual state before acting.\"}]},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"signature\":\"\",\"thinking\":\"\",\"type\":\"thinking\"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Got it. Here's what I've recorded:\\n\\n**CL-721 (Cedar Lantern)**, owner: Morgan, archive review Oct 18\\n- Rejected: auto-deleting imported notes.\\n- Archive originals. Store accepted summaries separately, each with its source ID.\\n- If summarization fails, keep the original.\\n- 30-day retention. Cleanup happens only at an explicit completed review, never when a request arrives.\\n- **Open:** attachments in the same archive or a separate one?\\n\\n**HF-934 (Harbor Finch)**, owner: Priya, rehearsal Oct 21\\n- Rejected: auto-retrying timed-out migrations.\\n- On timeout, check the ledger and retry only if the migration hasn't completed.\\n- Keep the exact migration ID and error.\\n- Rollback kept for 7 days.\\n- Verify child process state, not logs.\\n- **Open:** is the ledger in the app or the control DB?\\n\\nI haven't taken any actions. Once the two open questions are settled, I can draft the implementation notes.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Without using tools, recall both project names, diagnostic codes, owners, dates, rejected approaches and reasons. Explicitly identify the two unresolved questions. Do not invent a resolved answer.\"}]}]}","event":"request"}
